You can use `glob()` to get the files in a user's folder, then print them in an HTML table.

Example:

```php
<?php
$userFolder = "uploads/" . $userId . "/"; // build the user's directory

echo "<table border='1'>";
echo "<tr><th>File Name</th><th>Size</th></tr>";

foreach (glob($userFolder . "*") as $file) {
    if (is_file($file)) {
        echo "<tr>";
        echo "<td>" . htmlspecialchars(basename($file)) . "</td>";
        echo "<td>" . filesize($file) . " bytes</td>";
        echo "</tr>";
    }
}

echo "</table>";
?>
```

Notes:
- `glob($userFolder . "*")` lists all matching files.
- `is_file($file)` makes sure it’s actually a file.
- `basename($file)` gives just the filename.
- `htmlspecialchars()` helps prevent HTML injection when displaying names.

